Hieroglyph mapping attribution
=============================

The generated hieroglyph_data.zig mapping derives from the literal sign,
phonogram and simple atom-normalization maps in English Wiktionary's
Module:egy-hieroglyphs/data, revision 90914315 (22 May 2026), by Wiktionary
contributors:

https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Module:egy-hieroglyphs/data&oldid=90914315
https://en.wiktionary.org/w/index.php?title=Module:egy-hieroglyphs/data&action=history

The mapping attribution is retained under Creative Commons Attribution-
ShareAlike 4.0 International:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Changes: select single Unicode Gardiner signs and unambiguous literal phonetic
or simple atom aliases; sort the static data; omit complex, conflicting or
unrecognized syntax. The original captured source has SHA-256
407969a6e14aa3ab1ba133bf679556687b46ca89dbb5767dc24d0863ba6269fb.

Colon and asterisk joins follow the captured module's Unicode sign-join
controls U+13430 and U+13431; a dash separates adjacent signs without adding a
join control. This bounded conversion does not reproduce WikiHiero's complete
SVG layout, mirroring, enclosures or every Gardiner variant. Unknown input
keeps its readable source and unsupported-element diagnostic. Glyph/font and
spatial rendering require separate actual frontend review.
